              "China was once the world’s manufacturing hub. Those days are coming to an end. It doesn’t mean China’s manufacturing days are done. They will manufacturer for a home market, or their manufacturers will build abroad for that market, just like their U.S. counterparts",
              "But it was highly disruptive, with company towns from Massachusetts to Washington never quite the same since apparel and other manufacturers left town. China will experience similar growing pains over the next decade, but its consumer economy will continue to grow, changing the way investors think about the country.\n\nKraneShares thinks there will be weaker month-over-month economic data in the fourth quarter",
